      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "The sales and quoting process went seamlessly, but that's where the pleasant experience ended. I had to proactively contact the company to get updates on the status of my installation. The agreed-upon solar system was changed from a 6.6 kW system to a 5.6 kW system due to roof size constraints. After agreeing to the updated system, I was informed two days before installation that the panels were out of stock.The installation itself went relatively well, although one panel was scratched, and I am still waiting for a resolution on this issue. The solar system worked for less than a day before a fault appeared, which took three days to fix due to installation issues. The company failed to show up on the scheduled day without any communication and arrived two hours late the following day after several phone calls and messages from my end.The only proactive phone call I received from the owner was regarding payment. Three weeks have passed, and the system is still not connected to the grid.",
