      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "The battery is a Energizer HP-6M and HP-06, it is a phosphoric acid iron lithium salt battery, it is a 6.1kw system.Since installation it has been cloudy and raining and not ideal for solar generation, but the battery reports self sufficiency  at 94% for day 1, 64% for day 2 and 66% for day three.We are expecting much greater things when the sun final shines, we do live in the sunshine state.The installation was delayed a few weeks due to the need for Qld Government approval for rebate but once approval was gained the battery was installed a few days later.PDR took care of dealing with the grid power provider.One electrician and two apprentices did the installation, there were no dramas.The battery is mounted to a wall bracket and is not going anywhere it ways a ton ( 100+ kg ).There are two backup circuits of 15 Amps each when the power goes down.This is not the biggest battery in the world, it's primary use is to allow us to use our solar power during the day and night and also to keep our fridge and freezer alive during the next Queensland blackout.",
